      "body": "## What\n\nRequests that carry `token_indices_to_pool` (positional-readout / setwise scoring, as used by decision-model serving) must not be split by chunked prefill. When a batch fills past `--chunked-prefill-size` (default 8192), the last admitted request is chunked; its readout positions index the whole prompt, so they point past the chunk's hidden states and crash the scheduler with a CUDA `vectorized_gather_kernel` index-out-of-bounds assert.\n\nThe rule is 5 lines in `PrefillAdder._select_prefill_admission`: such a request returns `AddReqResult.OTHER` and waits for the next batch, as long as its prompt fits one chunk. Larger prompts keep today's behavior.\n\n## Why now\n\n#41712 (decision-model serving) generates these requests at concurrency and hit the crash in its first 32-way e2e run. The existing setwise e2e tests all run with `chunked_prefill_size=-1`, so this path was never exercised. Landing it separately keeps the serving PR reviewable.\n\n## Test\n\n`test_prefill_adder.py::test_readout_request_waits_instead_of_being_chunked` fails on the pre-fix code and passes with the fix. The 32-concurrent workload that produced the crash now completes with 0 errors.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:hourglass_flowing_sand: [Run #37881092051](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37881092051)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #37881091873](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37881091873)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:hourglass_flowing_sand: [Run #37881092072](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37881092072)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
